    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d347">

                <pb facs="0642" n="546" xml:id="pg546"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.6176 F 51/219: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Clark</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-08-19T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 19,
                                1926—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>25. For Bussell<anchor n="47" xml:id="d347-f1"/> from Castle. Since sending my
                    No. 24, August 11, 1 p.m.<anchor n="48" xml:id="d347-f2"/> the Department has
                    talked with Firestone who says <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“They will not accept Planting Agreement as passed by Legislature, but
                            that Harvey Firestone, Junior, is sailing immediately for Liberia in the
                            hope that satisfactory adjustments can be made and that if this is
                            accomplished they can lay out a program for Liberia which will be
                            helpful and progressive.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
